From 0135e7a732cbbef2a5d1b9f3e219518a4678c0c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duck-brain <duck-brain@localhost>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:04:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] duck-brain P21: a volume for the duck, and the vet book once
 a minute again

Alex's answers of 05.11.2026:
- [audio] volume, 0-1, linear (default 1): every sample robotd writes is
  multiplied by it - the fed wavs (bank sounds, robot.say phrases), the
  wheee segments, the theremin and the chorale. The duck's MAX98357A has
  no volume of its own. A wav that is not 16-bit PCM still goes to aplay
  as a file, unscaled.
- The vet book is saved once a minute again (P14 had made it five), on a
  clean stop as before, and also right before robotd powers the board
  off (low battery, robot.shutdown), in case the stop that follows does
  not get to it.
